    sampleAnswer: "White space is the empty area between and around design elements - it's not wasted space but an active design tool that improves readability (text with generous line spacing and margins is easier to read than cramped text), creates emphasis (isolating an element makes it stand out), and communicates a sense of quality or calm, which is why premium and minimalist brands typically use generous white space deliberately. A common mistake, especially under client pressure to \"fit more in,\" is treating white space as unused real estate to fill rather than as something actively working for the design's clarity and perceived quality.",
