    explanation: "",
    sampleAnswer: "Raise the concern directly and specifically rather than either quietly complying or refusing outright - explain the actual accessibility issue (a specific contrast ratio that fails WCAG, or a color-only status indicator that colorblind users can't parse), frame it in terms of real impact (a measurable share of users literally can't read or use it, and in many contexts there's legal/compliance exposure too, not just a design preference), and propose a specific alternative that still serves their creative intent as closely as possible. If the client still insists on proceeding after understanding the trade-off, document that the concern was raised and the decision was made with that information, rather than silently overriding their explicit choice or simply refusing to deliver the work.",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nRaise the concern directly and specifically rather than either quietly complying or refusing outright - explain the actual accessibility issue (a specific contrast ratio that fails WCAG, or a color-only status indicator that colorblind users can't parse), frame it in terms of real impact (a measurable share of users literally can't read or use it, and in many contexts there's legal/compliance exposure too, not just a design preference), and propose a specific alternative that still serves their creative intent as closely as possible. If the client still insists on proceeding after understanding the trade-off, document that the concern was raised and the decision was made with that information, rather than silently overriding their explicit choice or simply refusing to deliver the work.\n\n**Example:**\n\nA client wants light-gray text on a white background for a minimalist look that fails contrast requirements. Rather than just saying no, showing them the exact contrast ratio, a mockup of how it will actually appear to a significant share of users, and a slightly darker gray alternative that keeps the same minimalist feel usually resolves it without a confrontation.",
