    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nA credible answer names specific, ongoing habits rather than a vague claim of \"always learning\" - following specific design communities, publications, or practitioners whose work is relevant to your specialization, regularly analyzing work you admire to understand why it works rather than just appreciating it passively, doing small personal projects to practice techniques or tools outside of client constraints, and staying current with the specific software and platform updates relevant to your work (new features in your primary design tools, changes in how a target platform renders content).\n\n**Example:**\n\nA UI-focused designer might mention following specific product design case studies and community critique groups, regularly rebuilding a small personal interface concept to try out new interaction patterns, and staying current with a specific design tool's plugin ecosystem and release notes rather than a generic claim of following 'design trends.'",
