    explanation: "",
    sampleAnswer: "Start with discovery before any visual work: understand the business, its target audience, its competitive landscape, and what the brand wants to be known for, since starting from visual exploration before this groundwork risks producing something that looks good in isolation but doesn't actually fit the business or resonate with its audience. From there, define a small set of guiding attributes or a positioning statement the visual identity should express, explore multiple genuinely distinct visual directions grounded in that positioning (rather than one direction refined in isolation), and build the system out (logo, color, type, imagery style) once a direction is validated, documenting it into usable guidelines as the final deliverable, not an afterthought.",
    detailedAnswer: "**Direct answer:**\n\nStart with discovery before any visual work: understand the business, its target audience, its competitive landscape, and what the brand wants to be known for, since starting from visual exploration before this groundwork risks producing something that looks good in isolation but doesn't actually fit the business or resonate with its audience. From there, define a small set of guiding attributes or a positioning statement the visual identity should express, explore multiple genuinely distinct visual directions grounded in that positioning (rather than one direction refined in isolation), and build the system out (logo, color, type, imagery style) once a direction is validated, documenting it into usable guidelines as the final deliverable, not an afterthought.\n\n**Example:**\n\nBuilding an identity for a new sustainable packaging startup would start with understanding their target customers (eco-conscious retailers vs. individual consumers changes the direction significantly), then explore a few distinct positioning-driven directions - one more clinical/scientific, one more warm/artisanal - before committing to and fully building out whichever direction tests best with the actual target audience.",
